# lottie-forge — line-ending policy
#
# Force LF for ALL tracked text files on checkout, regardless of the
# platform's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, `git clone` on Windows
# converts LF (the committed form) to CRLF on checkout via autocrlf=true,
# and the Biome formatter rejects the CRLF files with "Formatter would
# have printed..." warnings — a fresh-checkout on Windows would fail the
# local verification chain while the CI (ubuntu-latest) would pass.
#
# The repo's canonical form is LF (the GitHub Actions runner is Linux,
# biome defaults to platform-native but auto-resolves to LF on non-Windows
# hosts and CRLF on Windows — diverging by environment).
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect binary vs text, `eol=lf` enforces the
# checkout form. We keep `*` broad because every text file in the repo is
# authored to expect LF.

* text=auto eol=lf